<div class="sec alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><span class="eyebrow rv">Frequently asked</span><h2 class="split">Questions we hear most</h2></div>
<div class="rv">
<details><summary>How quickly can a project start?</summary><p>Most projects start within two to three weeks of the first call, after a short discovery workshop to agree scope and team.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you work with our in-house team?</summary><p>Yes. We can embed with your engineers, lead delivery end to end, or mix both.</p></details>
<details><summary>Who owns the code?</summary><p>You do, from day one. Code, documentation and infrastructure definitions live in your repositories, not ours.</p></details>
<details><summary>Which technologies do you use?</summary><p>Modern web, mobile, cloud and data stacks. Tell us yours, and we'll say honestly if it's outside our strengths.</p></details>
<details><summary>Which time zones do you cover?</summary><p>Our team works from India (IST). We agree overlapping working hours and meeting times with your team at kickoff.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will you sign an NDA?</summary><p>Yes, before we see anything confidential.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if we want to stop?</summary><p>Give us 30 days' notice. We hand over code, documentation and access, and walk your team through it. No lock-in.</p></details>
</div></div></div>
